// Gate a whole action GROUP with one information provider. The rule is
// scoped `action in [Drupe::Action::"CallTool"]` — the group — rather
// than a single `action == …`. The provider's hoisted
// `context.providers.<id>` field is declared on every action's context and
// evaluated for every decision event, so the same guardrail applies to
// both descendants (`Read`, `Post`) without duplicating the rule per
// action; the group scope decides which requests the RULE fires for.
//
// This exercises the group case end to end: a request for either
// descendant action evaluates the provider and is permitted only when the
// document id is all-uppercase letters.

permit (
    principal,
    action in [Drupe::Action::"CallTool"],
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Strings::Matches(context.input.document, "^[A-Z]+$").matched == true
};
